      "cooked": "<p>Hi</p>\n<p>Frappe Cloud site URL</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">test.frappe.cloud\n</code></pre>\n<p>I can get to the login screen by type the URL just above</p>\n<p>However, I want to access it by using a URL, managed at my domains<br>\nservice provider. The URL that I want to use …</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">test.example.com\n</code></pre>\n<p>So, I modify the DNS records at my service provider ( I tried two ways )</p>\n<p>First try…</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">test.example.com ....600 ... CNAME ....... test.frappe.cloud\n</code></pre>\n<p>Second try …</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">test.example.com ..... 600 ....A..........10.11.12.13\n</code></pre>\n<p>where 10.11.12.13 is the inbound IP found on my Frappe console</p>\n<p>But both these take me to the control panel for  test.frappe.cloud, not to the<br>\nlogin screen ???</p>\n<p>All my efforts based on this doc…<br>\n<a href=\"https://frappecloud.com/docs/sites/custom-domains\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://frappecloud.com/docs/sites/custom-domains</a></p>",
